{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"toolshed_web_search","tool":"call_web_search","arguments":{"web_search_instructions":"Prodigi API sandbox create order t-shirt product SKU print on demand v4 product catalog documentation"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Research Report: Prodigi API v4 Documentation for Creating T-Shirt Orders with Product SKUs\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nThe Prodigi API v4 provides a comprehensive framework for integrating print-on-demand services, including the creation of t-shirt orders using specific product SKUs. This report outlines the steps to authenticate, select products, and submit orders through the API, ensuring seamless integration for developers.\n\n## Key Findings\n\n- **Finding 1:** Prodigi offers both sandbox and live environments for API integration, allowing developers to test orders without incurring charges before moving to production. ([prodigi.com](https://www.prodigi.com/print-api/docs/reference/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Finding 2:** To create an order, developers must authenticate using an API key, specify the shipping method, provide recipient details, and include order items with the appropriate SKU and image assets. ([prodigi.com](https://www.prodigi.com/blog/your-first-print-api-order/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Finding 3:** The API supports various t-shirt products, each identified by a unique SKU, with specific attributes such as color and size that must be specified when placing an order. ([dashboard.dev.kitely.prodigi.tech](https://dashboard.dev.kitely.prodigi.tech/docs/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Finding 4:** Prodigi provides detailed documentation and resources, including a Postman collection, to assist developers in integrating and testing the API effectively. ([prodigi.com](https://www.prodigi.com/print-api/docs/?utm_source=openai))\n\n---\n\n## Detailed Source Analysis\n\n### Source 1: Prodigi API Documentation\n\n- **URL:** ([prodigi.com](https://www.prodigi.com/print-api/docs/reference/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Domain:** prodigi.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** Date not specified\n\n- **Source Type:** Official Documentation\n\n- **Credibility:** High (Official source from Prodigi)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThe Prodigi API v4 documentation provides a comprehensive guide to integrating print-on-demand services. It details the RESTful API structure, including standard HTTP response codes, authentication methods, and supported HTTP verbs. The documentation emphasizes the availability of both sandbox and live environments, allowing developers to test their integrations without processing actual orders. Authentication is managed through an `X-API-Key` header, which can be obtained by creating a free Prodigi account. The order creation process involves specifying shipping methods, recipient details, and order items, each identified by a unique SKU. The API also supports branding options and metadata inclusion for orders.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Sandbox API URL: `https://api.sandbox.prodigi.com`\n\n- Live API URL: `https://api.prodigi.com`\n\n- Authentication header: `X-API-Key`\n\n- Order object includes fields like `id`, `created`, `branding`, `items`, and `metadata`\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"Creating an order is a single API request, supplying all of the relevant information.\"\n\n> \"We have two environments: Sandbox and Live.\"\n\n---\n\n### Source 2: How to Place Your First Order with the Prodigi Print API\n\n- **URL:** ([prodigi.com](https://www.prodigi.com/blog/your-first-print-api-order/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Domain:** prodigi.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** March 18, 2021\n\n- **Source Type:** Blog Post\n\n- **Credibility:** High (Official blog post from Prodigi)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThis blog post serves as a step-by-step guide for placing an order using the Prodigi API v4. It outlines the process of acquiring an API key by creating an account, selecting a product by its SKU, sourcing an appropriate image asset, and submitting the order through a POST request to the API. The guide emphasizes the importance of using the sandbox environment for testing purposes and provides code examples for each step. It also highlights the need to specify the correct image dimensions and resolutions to ensure print quality.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Example SKU: `GLOBAL-FAP-16x24`\n\n- Recommended image resolution: 4800x7200 pixels for a 16x24\" print\n\n- API endpoint for order creation: `/v4.0/orders/`\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"First, create an account. This will give you access to both our sandbox and live environments.\"\n\n> \"We accept jpg and png format images.\"\n\n---\n\n### Source 3: Print API Reference\n\n- **URL:** ([dashboard.dev.kitely.prodigi.tech](https://dashboard.dev.kitely.prodigi.tech/docs/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Domain:** prodigi.tech\n\n- **Publication Date:** Date not specified\n\n- **Source Type:** Technical Documentation\n\n- **Credibility:** High (Official technical documentation)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThe Print API Reference provides detailed information on product templates, including t-shirts, available through the Prodigi API. It lists various t-shirt products identified by unique SKUs, along with their applicable print positions, available colors, and sizes. The documentation specifies the required image dimensions for each print area to ensure optimal print quality. It also outlines the attributes that must be specified when placing an order, such as color and size, to match the selected product template.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Example t-shirt SKU: `aa_mens_tshirt`\n\n- Available colors: black, white, heather_grey\n\n- Available sizes: s, m, l, xl\n\n- Print area dimensions: 2100 x 2400 px (30x40cm) for center_chest and center_back\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"All apparel orders must be made with options and sizes that correspond to the product ordered as detailed in the below table.\"\n\n> \"center_chest optional | Image: T-Shirt Print API Centre Chest | 2100 x 2400 px (30x40cm)\"\n\n---\n\n## Cross-Reference Analysis\n\n**Consensus Across Sources:**\n\n- All sources agree on the necessity of obtaining an API key and using the `X-API-Key` header for authentication. ([prodigi.com](https://www.prodigi.com/print-api/docs/reference/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- The importance of using the sandbox environment for testing orders before moving "}],"_meta":{"openai/widgetSessionId":"e6d6fdbe-44d5-4c57-95b9-687d83b62790"},"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
